# Atlas Technology Stack

<!-- merged from: atlas/01-atlas-technology-stack -->

Do not change the stack without an explicit architectural decision record.

## Zones

| Zone | Runtime | Key libraries |
|---|---|---|
| Zone 2 — Experiences | Next.js 16 App Router, React 19, TypeScript | MUI v5+, React Query, Zustand, RHF + Zod, Playwright |
| Zone 3 — Platform | Node 20, Fastify, Neo4j driver, Zod, Vitest | |
| Zone 5 — AI | Python 3.11+, FastAPI, Pydantic v2, pytest | Azure OpenAI |
| Zone 4 — Data | Neo4j, Blob, Redis, Service Bus | |
| Zone 1 — Auth Proxy | Node 20, Fastify, MS Entra ID, Redis sessions | |

## AI model rule

- Runtime model and provider selection must come from Neo4j `(:AIModel)` and `(:PromptTemplate)` nodes.
- Do not hardcode model names, parameters, or provider-specific defaults in application code.
- Voice uses the Realtime API (WebSocket / WebRTC).

## Hard constraints

- TypeScript strict mode everywhere.
- Python type hints required on all functions.
- No stack swaps: no Fluent UI for new code, no Chakra / Redux / Jest / Prisma / Postgres / Auth0 / GraphQL.
- MUI is the UI library for all new Zone 2 code.
